-- examples/checks/agg-datastrat-neg.rofl — A NEGATION INSIDE THE AGGREGATE'S BODY
-- reads the component as a premise does: the count of a key's items that are not
-- flagged waits for the flags, and a flag is raised by another key's count.
--   key a has item x, key b has item y; b's flag-raiser names x.
--   c(b) = 1 (y is not flagged), so x is flagged, so c(a) = 0.
-- A count that read `not flag(X)` as holding would seal c(a) at 1 before the
-- flag existed (a wrong number, and a member gone after the seal).
edb(key). edb(item). edb(flagme).
key(a). key(b).
item(a, x). item(b, y).
flagme(b, x).
c(K, N) :- key(K), N is count(X : item(K, X), not flag(X)).
flag(X) :- c(K, N), N > 0, flagme(K, X).
